# Frontend Design Rules

## State Management

Separate concerns by state origin:

| State Type | Tool | Rule |
|------------|------|------|
| Server state | TanStack Query / SWR / tRPC | Cache with stale-while-revalidate. Never copy server state into client stores. |
| Client state | Zustand / Jotai / signals | Only UI-specific state (theme, sidebar open, form draft). Keep it minimal. |
| URL state | searchParams, route params | Shareable state (filters, sort, page, active tab) belongs in the URL. |
| Form state | React Hook Form / Zod | Validate with schema. Submit via server action or mutation hook. |

## Data Fetching

- Stale-while-revalidate paradigm: show cached data immediately, refetch in background
- Parallel loading: fetch independent data in parallel (not in parent-child waterfall)
- Prefetch likely next routes (link hover, viewport entry)
- Optimistic updates: snapshot → apply → rollback on error → show toast on failure
- Error boundaries for each data-fetching section (don't crash the whole page)

## Bundle Budget

| Page Type | JS Budget (gzipped) | CSS Budget |
|-----------|---------------------|------------|
| Landing page | < 150KB | < 30KB |
| App page | < 300KB | < 50KB |
| Microsite | < 80KB | < 15KB |

- Enforce budget in CI. Fail builds that exceed budget.
- Dynamic import heavy libraries: `const ThreeScene = await import('./ThreeScene')`
- Route-based code splitting mandatory for all SPA routes
- Analyze bundle composition: `npx vite-bundle-analyzer` or `nextjs bundle-analyzer`

## Core Web Vitals Targets

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) | < 2.5s |
| First Input Delay (INP) | < 200ms |
| Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) | < 0.1 |
| First Contentful Paint (FCP) | < 1.5s |
| Time to Interactive (TTI) | < 3.8s |

## Component Architecture

- Container/Presentational separation: containers load data, presenters render UI
- Compound components for related widgets (Tabs, Select, Accordion)
- Custom hooks for reusable stateful logic (not HOCs or render props)
- Server components by default (Next.js); client components only when interactivity is needed

## TypeScript Rules (for Frontend)

- `strict: true` in tsconfig
- Props typed with `interface` (extendable)
- No `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow with type guards.
- Discriminated unions for state machine patterns
- Zod schemas for runtime validation at API boundaries

## CSS Methodology

| Approach | When to Use | Avoid |
|----------|-------------|-------|
| Tailwind CSS | Utility-first for layout, spacing, typography. Default choice. | `@apply` for everything — extract repeated patterns only |
| CSS Modules | Scoped class names, component-local styles, `composes:` for shared | Global styles leaking via `:global` |
| styled-components | Dynamic props-driven styling (runtime theme switching) | Performance-sensitive pages (runtime overhead) |
| vanilla-extract / linaria | Zero-runtime CSS-in-JS, type-safe design tokens | Projects where Tailwind is already established |

- Responsive: `sm:` / `md:` / `lg:` / `xl:` Tailwind breakpoints, or `@media` queries for CSS Modules.
- Design tokens as CSS custom properties: `--color-surface`, `--text-base`, `--space-section`.
- No inline styles except for genuinely dynamic values (e.g., progress bar width).

## Component Library & Design System

- **shadcn/ui**: Copy/modify pattern. Best for custom design systems. Not a dependency.
- **Radix UI / Ark UI**: Headless primitives. Full style control, full accessibility built in.
- **MUI / Ant Design**: Full design systems. Use when design velocity > customization needs.
- **Storybook / Histoire**: Isolated component development + visual regression testing.
- Design tokens as single source of truth → CSS custom properties → shared with design tools (Figma).
- Compound component pattern for complex widgets: `<Select.Trigger>`, `<Select.Options>` etc.

## Form Design Patterns

- React Hook Form (RHF) + Zod for schema validation — default approach.
- Uncontrolled inputs by default (better performance). Controlled only for conditional fields.
- Validation strategies: `onBlur` (standard), `onChange` (real-time feedback), `onSubmit` (fallback).
- Server-side validation errors must be merged back into client form state via `setError`.
- File upload: drag-and-drop zone + chunked upload + blob storage. Show progress bar.
- Form accessibility: every input has `<label>`, errors linked via `aria-describedby`.

## Internationalization (i18n)

- **next-intl** (Next.js), **react-i18next** (React), **vue-i18n** (Vue) — framework-native solutions.
- All user-visible strings stored in `locales/<lang>.json`. Zero hardcoded UI strings.
- Type-safe message keys: `@formatjs/cli` (React) or `typesafe-i18n`.
- ICU message syntax for plurals, gender, and nesting: `{count, plural, =1 {1 item} other {# items}}`.
- RTL support: `dir="rtl"` + logical CSS properties (`margin-inline-start` not `margin-left`).
- Date/number formatting: `Intl.DateTimeFormat` / `Intl.NumberFormat` — locale-aware.

## Icons, Images, Fonts

### Icons
- `lucide-react` / `lucide-vue` — tree-shakeable, consistent design, 1000+ icons.
- Custom SVG: sprite sheet with `<use href="/sprite.svg#icon-name">`. Avoid inline `<svg>` duplication.
- SVGR for importing SVGs as React components when custom styling is required.
- All icons: `aria-hidden="true"` (decorative) or `aria-label="icon name"` (informative).

### Images
- Next.js `<Image>` (auto-optimize) or manual `<picture>` with AVIF/WebP sources.
- Always set explicit `width` and `height` — prevents Cumulative Layout Shift.
- `loading="lazy"` for below-fold. `fetchpriority="high"` for hero only.
- Responsive `srcset` with at least 3 breakpoints (mobile, tablet, desktop).

### Fonts
- `next/font` for self-hosted variable fonts, `@fontsource` for npm packages.
- Preload critical font weights (400, 700 for body; custom weights for headings).
- `font-display: swap` mandatory. Accept FOUT, never FOIT.
- Maximum 2 font families per project unless justified.

